{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_ZpovlXXcqBtElaEypFXeLthe","content":"1\t---\n2\tmilestone: cross-document-growth\n3\tstation: phase-CG3\n4\tscope: phase-CG3\n5\tskill: \"n/a -- repository development, not a gnd-solve station over a domain model\"\n6\tdate: 2026-11-28\n7\tgates:\n8\t  - command: \"pytest -q tests/test_consolidation_loop.py --tb=short\"\n9\t    exit: 0\n10\t  - command: \"pytest -q tests/test_consolidation_loop.py tests/test_rf6_query_policy.py --tb=short\"\n11\t    exit: 0\n12\t  - command: \"ruff check .\"\n13\t    exit: 0\n14\t  - command: \"python3 scripts/components_index.py --no-cache changed --base 1cce6979 --strict\"\n15\t    exit: 0\n16\tevidence:\n17\t  - path: tests/test_consolidation_loop.py\n18\t    sha256: 8d6b728550efe0679efc7966008e9aaa9899c2cc468642659a4edea3ab3c3580\n19\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/cross-document-growth/notes/reviews/CG3-r1/independent-review.md\n20\t    sha256: d7e3815c0a475597fe9c37a78d1864255aeef4fe179387cf946c4fa0181a8b16\n21\tslow_cadence: 'uv run pytest -q -m \"evidence or census\"'\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\tDelegated acceptance (auto=true) on November 28, 2026. The CG3 terminal workflow supports leave, merge, demote to row and subtype link. The integrated two-document sample replay and the uninterrupted/interrupted equivalence test are described in [closure evidence](notes/close-delta.md). The decision journal records the whole proposal before mutation. Role references, constraint preservation, located sample multisets, source locations and model CAS guard the mutation. A pre-publication stale intent is superseded only before evidence staging.\n25\t\n26\tFocused result: 16 passed in 10.13s. The post-repair focused and RF6 checks returned 32 passed in 17.73s before the directory-alias regression was added. The phase structure, CLI, packaging, install, doctor, disclosure and CG1–3 selection on the earlier implementation returned 1053 passed, 2 deselected in 170.41s. A separately installed offline wheel ran the packaged terminal example and recorded one leave before reporting a different group. The wheel test preceded the final review repairs.\n27\t\n28\t## Independent review and refactoring\n29\t\n30\tThe [review](notes/reviews/CG3-r1/independent-review.md) found two group-scope issues, two evidence-loss paths, a stale-intent recovery defect and a path alias defect. The [ledger](notes/reviews/CG3-r1/FINDINGS.md) binds each disposition to a repair. One reviewer is one reviewer. The source constraint loss case separately failed before repair. Shared sample population evaluation now serves both additive admission and the reviewed mutation check. The existing evolution service owns publication, conformance and recovery. The strict component check reported no fixes or warnings; the existing evolution subsystem and population admission descriptions still apply.\n31\t\n32\t## Boundary\n33\t\n34\tThe journal and model directory are locally trusted. The workflow needs POSIX directory locking for journal writers. Divergence after staging requires reconciliation. Referenced external populations require separate review. The replay simulates process interruption at publication and finalization boundaries. Real hardware power loss was not tested."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_Hu18582nElsQ1DgJfKgy9Ysa","content":"1\t# Cross-document growth closure evidence\n2\t\n3\tThe public entry points are additive evolution preview and apply with repeatable sample document inputs, consolidate candidates, and the installed gnd-consolidate terminal skill. The product changed on the milestone branch. Issues #338 and #339 remain open pending merge into the default branch.\n4\t\n5\t## Replay\n6\t\n7\tThe integrated test in tests/test_consolidation_loop.py takes a valid unattended model, supplies bytes for a second document and appends an already-observed tuple from its distinct cited occurrence. It uses the public preview and apply commands before discovery. It then reviews the candidate group and submits one digest-bound proposal with a row move and a deletion. The surviving fact contains both source locations for the same typed tuple. The role rewrite test merges two object types, preserves the sample and rejects rewrites to an unrelated third type.\n8\t\n9\tThe recovery comparison runs the same leave and merge in separate temporary workspaces. It injects an interruption at finalization after the model CAS. A subsequent invocation without a decision completes the journal. It compares the complete model bytes, all durable decision fields (including IDs and work counters), and the resulting report and terminal reason. A separate stale-input control, a deontic constraint conflict, and an incomplete transfer leave original model bytes intact. Changing the supporting source of a declined group offers it again.\n10\t\n11\t## Boundaries\n12\t\n13\tThe reporter's two large models were unavailable. The score is a discovery heuristic. No paid grower effectiveness trial was selected. Local samples and source provenance establish the checks' scope. Mutations use one reviewed proposal and the existing evolution transaction. The final record reports conformance status separately. CG2's independent review changed the evidence representation to exclude guessable row-value hashes. The group evidence digest covers the location and public evidence emitted. A decision independently commits to the entire reviewed model."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_PYyGSfr2vdyEfezqfZwyUmRU","content":"1\t# Cross-document model growth\n2\t\n3\tRevision 2, 2026-11-28. The owner delegated milestone rulings and selected the light panel. All six reviewers assessed revision 1. The changes below carry the coordinator’s disposition of those findings. Completion requires the phase results below and a separate milestone-close ruling.\n4\t\n5\t## 0. Binding design rules\n6\t\n7\tDocument and check every new sample span against the cited document before CAS. Count duplicate evidence separately from distinct rows. Use existing loaders, ModelIndex for model queries and the defining component for policy. State validation order at each public boundary and test both sides of every refusal.\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Scope, sources and authority\n10\t\n11\tIssue requirements come from [#338](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/338), [#339](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/339), including their proposed changes and reproduction examples. Implementation baseline 83cd4170. The [predecessor close](../../compact-growth-context/004-milestone-close.md) records the inherited capability and the limits of its evidence. These are framework features; a domain experiment census cannot establish API or evaluator behavior.\n12\t\n13\t## 2. Proposed behavior\n14\t\n15\tAppend located rows to a locally owned fact under additive preview and apply. Keep prior rows and spans intact and validate the extended population.\n16\t\n17\tIndex singleton types, role-player and reading shapes, name similarity, units and counted nouns. Emit stable candidate IDs, evidence locations and scores. Reordering declarations must preserve groups.\n18\t\n19\tReview one group at a time against source spans. Preview row moves and role rewrites together, record merge, demotion, subtype or leave, recompute candidates after apply and stop at the configured threshold.\n20\t\n21\t## 3. Dependencies and artifact homes\n22\t\n23\tCG1 provides the canonical evidence representation for CG2 and CG3. Candidate discovery may read a model before CG1 ships, but the closure replay must exercise two documents and an accepted merge. Start with [src/gnd/evolve/policy.py](../../../../src/gnd/evolve/policy.py). The component index identifies `evolve.policy`, `evolve.population_check`, `evolve.service`, `evolve.round_summary`. Its November 27 review flagged 105 descriptions older than their source; resolve contract details against code and tests.\n24\t\n25\t## 4. Obligations and completion criteria\n26\t\n27\t| Phase | Issue and deliverable | Observable exit criterion |\n28\t|---|---|---|\n29\t| CG1 | [#338](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/338) Located additions | Append located rows to a locally owned fact under additive preview and apply. Keep prior rows and spans intact and validate the extended population. |\n30\t| CG2 | [#339](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/339) Candidate discovery | Index singleton types, role-player and reading shapes, name similarity, units and counted nouns. Emit stable candidate IDs, evidence locations and scores. Reordering declarations must preserve groups. |\n31\t| CG3 | [#339](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/339) Reviewed consolidation loop | Review one group at a time against source spans. Preview row moves and role rewrites together, record merge, demotion, subtype or leave, recompute candidates after apply and stop at the configured threshold. |\n32\t\n33\tThe [first draft spec](phase-CG1-spec.md) expands CG1. Later specs follow the preceding decisions. Carry the predecessor’s documented limits into each new public claim.\n34\t\n35\t## 5. Documentation and compatibility\n36\t\n37\tGrowth policy currently directs later rows to open questions. Changing that public guidance belongs to CG1. CG3 owns the packaged consolidation skill and its installed example. Start from [docs/reference/evolve-policy.md](../../../../docs/reference/evolve-policy.md). Run existing examples and compare the observable result for a caller using the previous interface.\n38\t\n39\t## 6. Risks and controls\n40\t\n41\tDocument and check every new sample span against the cited document before CAS. Count duplicate evidence separately from distinct rows. Vary identifiers, declaration order and input cardinality in the acceptance fixtures. Record work counters and the first refusal where limits apply.\n42\t\n43\t## 7. Outside this milestone\n44\t\n45\tPaid grower effectiveness and cross-model alignment. Release scheduling belongs to the owner.\n46\t\n47\t## 8. Execution and review\n48\t\n49\tEach phase needs its own spec and owner ruling, implementation, focused tests, independent diff review, refactoring review and numbered record. Plan and close require the project’s four-reviewer bar, recorded against the reviewed bytes. The owner selects the panel. Merge and release have separate authority.\n50\t\n51\t## 9. Verification and baseline\n52\t\n53\tObserved at intake: Existing guidance sends later rows to open questions. The compact inventory identifies vocabulary but omits sample rows. The corpus counts in #338 and #339 come from the reporter.\n54\t\n55\tRun the first spec’s focused selection and retain its verbatim pytest summary. For each later phase, use the issue reproduction and the criterion in §4 as an acceptance pair, pin the old behavior on unextended inputs and record the public entry point and result. Milestone closure requires a replay across phases, a disposition for each issue and an inventory of unverified claims. Native backend claims require native execution.\n56\t\n57\tCG2: shuffle model declaration order and compare candidate group IDs and cited spans. Include two similarly named types with incompatible role players; the suggestion must carry evidence for review. CG3: accept one group, decline another, restart from the decision log and verify that the declined group is not offered again unless its evidence changes. After a rename or deletion validate all role references and locate every transferred row’s original source.\n58\t\n59\t## 10. Open decisions\n60\t\n61\tThe delegated decision adopts append-only samples for root-owned facts. Included definitions stay owned by their source. A host may record evidence for an included fact as an open question. The earlier alternative of a separate growth population remains in revision 1 at ecb01fa9.\n62\t\n63\t## Amendment after plan review\n64\t\n65\t1. CG1 uses an explicit document input. A caller supplies source bytes for appended spans at preview and apply. Validate authored root ownership, preserve every old row and span, check declared document identity and excerpt against supplied bytes, then validate the candidate samples with the ordinary population reader and checker. An affected constraint must return pass. Any missing coverage, warning, violation, or evaluator inability refuses the operation. Retain ordinary CAS validation and the original model on failure. Exercise root and included targets and a deontic uniqueness warning. Provide the public guidance and the fallback for sources lacking sufficient evidence.\n66\t2. Treat an indexed sample as an observation. An additional document may support an identical tuple; preserve the located observation and evaluate the distinct typed facts. A repeated identical tuple and source occurrence adds no evidence and is refused as redundant. An existing preview applied again follows the existing transaction recovery contract. Test differing excerpts and differing documents separately.\n67\t3. CG2 owns deterministic candidate discovery. Define stable identity from the signal, root-owned member kind and sorted member IDs. Hash the sorted evidence (including source digests and locations) separately so a newly supported group can be reconsidered without changing its identity. Include one true candidate and one control for singleton entities, role-player signatures, reading shapes, similar names, units and counted nouns. Include cross-document and renamed fixtures. Discovery is advisory and never applies a candidate. Charge indexed items and examined candidate pairs, return incomplete on budget exhaustion, and test exact-budget and one-less boundaries.\n68\t4. CG3 reviews candidates with one of four decisions: leave, demote to row, merge or link subtype. Bind each decision to group and evidence hashes and the reviewed model digest. A leave suppresses only the same evidence. A mutation uses one digest-bound proposal for the entire group, including row moves and role rewrites. Check constraint conflicts and dangling references before applying. Persist proposal and decision identity before publishing, and complete the existing transaction on recovery. Demonstrate failed rewrites leave both rows and references intact and restart after publication completes the ledger once. Bound the loop by maximum decisions and discovery work. Terminate when no eligible unresolved group meets the selected minimum score, the budget expires, or a decision needs input. Record the reason explicitly.\n69\t5. Milestone closure replays two source documents, a duplicate observation, one accepted group, one declined group and an interrupted restart. Compare the final model digest, surviving references, located evidence, decision identities, counters and terminal reason between uninterrupted and resumed runs. Preserve origin spans during transfers and refuse conflicting constraints. Put the replay and exact results in the milestone close record.\n70\t\n71\tThe [first panel report](plan-review-r1.md) preserves every agreed and divergent finding. The runtime homes and baseline discrepancy are checked in [execution intake](execution-intake.md). The five amendment clauses supersede shorthand in the phase table. One plan round was budgeted before implementation; use focused code tests to settle runtime behavior."}
